{"WINQ_AUTUMN","reg=civilian,family,worker,rescue|st=friendly,neutral",{"Winter's coming, I can smell it, a metallic tang in the air","Get your firewood now, because later it's too late","I'm stocking up like a squirrel, nuts, berries, tin cans","It's going to be a hard one, the farmers say, by the thickness of the corn husks","The geese are flying south, early, a bad sign","I'm dreading it, honestly, and I'm preparing for it","Last winter was brutal, and this one will be worse","Gather what you can, patch what you can, pray for the rest","Pack extra blankets, extra socks, extra everything","Winter's a hungry beast, and it's headed our way","I hope we're ready","Everything takes twice as long in the cold, plan for it"}},
